  "decision": "dependency_refresh_race_fix_verified",
  "problem": "Delayed require refresh could restore corrected errors, clear newer missing requires, publish after close or into a replacement project, ignore newly opened project targets, and erase current syntax/linter output.",
  "changes": [
    "Capture opaque engine-owned source snapshots; reject stale require-diagnostic replacements, including empty clears.",
    "Acquire the existing document semantic lock, retain longest-root workspace ownership and immutable dependency-index identity through commit and synchronous publication, and recheck source/indexing generation.",
    "Collect complete static requires from the current open buffer, using masked Ruby for templates, and resolve against current engine project targets at commit time.",
    "Closed consumers reuse stored missing-require facts without disk rereads or publication. Open consumers publish complete syntax, semantic, and exact-source linter diagnostics without rerunning the linter.",
    "Checkpoint the coordinator around dependency-root publication and after the awaited refresh."
  ],
